---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **그룹 멤버를 생년 × 성별로 센 지면.** (`/service-years`)
 *
 * ── 🔴 이 지면이 지키는 것 — 지우지 않는다 ──────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **입대를 예측하지 않는다.** 우리는 입대 날짜를 쥔 적이 없다. 이름 옆에 「입대 예정」을 안 쓴다
 * ⛔ **병역법의 나이 규정을 단정하지 않는다.** 법은 우리 자료가 아니다
 * ⛔ **국적을 말하지 않는다.** 태어난 곳은 국적이 아니고, 대부분 안 적혀 있다
 * ⛔ 「남성 멤버 명단」을 따로 뽑아 내지 않는다 — 그러면 「입대 예정자 명단」으로 읽힌다.
 *    해별 수를 내고, 이름은 성별과 «함께» 낸다
 * ⚠ 나이는 움직이는 수다 — 생년(안 변하는 것)과 기준 해를 «같이» 적는다.
 *   `build-kcw-age-bands.mjs` 가 이미 겪은 함정이다
 * ⛔ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `kcw-service-years.json` 에서 읽는다
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import data from '../../data/kcw-service-years.json';

const 해 = data.asOfYear;
const 있는해 = data.byYear.filter((y) => y.전체 > 0);
/* 스물 몇 살 구간 — 손님이 이 지면에 오는 까닭이 여기다. ⛔ 법을 말하지 않고 나이만 말한다 */
const 이십대후반 = 있는해.filter((y) => y.해나이 >= 24 && y.해나이 <= 30);
const 남성합 = 이십대후반.reduce((a, y) => a + y.남성, 0);
const 가장많은해 = [...있는해].sort((a, b) => b.남성 - a.남성)[0];
const 성별율 = Math.round((data.men + data.women) / data.distinctPeopleWithBirthYear * 100);

const TITLE = `${data.men} men and ${data.women} women across ${data.groupsRead} K-pop groups, by birth year`;
const DESC =
  `Every member of ${data.groupsRead} Korean music groups with a recorded date of birth — `
  + `${data.distinctPeopleWithBirthYear} people — counted by birth year and by sex as recorded on Wikidata. `
  + `${남성합} of the men were born in the years that turn 24 to 30 during ${해}. `
  + `No enlistment dates, no predictions: the counts only.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: String(해),
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.wikidata.org'],
  variableMeasured: ['birth year', 'sex or gender as recorded', 'group membership'],
};
const 수 = (v) => (v == null ? '—' : Number(v).toLocaleString('en-US'));
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/service-years">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Wikidata records the members of {data.groupsRead} Korean music groups. {수(data.memberSlots)} of those
    membership slots resolve to {수(data.distinctPeopleWithBirthYear)} distinct people with a date of
    birth — a person in two groups is counted once. This page puts them on two axes we can actually
    read off that source: the year they were born, and the sex or gender an editor recorded.
  </p>

  <p class="warn">
    <b>What this page will not do.</b> It will not tell you who enlists, or when. We hold no
    enlistment dates, no discharge dates, and no citizenship. Korean military obligation applies to
    male citizens, and we can establish neither citizenship nor obligation from this data — so we
    print the counts and stop. The arithmetic below is yours to use.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Ages move, birth years do not</h2>
    <p class="note lead-in">
      <b>How to read the table.</b> Every age here is the age a person reaches during <b>{해}</b>.
      A page rebuilt next year would move every age by one, so the birth year is printed beside it —
      that column never changes. If you are reading this in a later year, add the difference yourself.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Born</th><th>Turns this age in {해}</th><th>Men</th><th>Women</th>
            <th>Sex not recorded</th><th>Members</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="edge">
            <td class="nm">All years</td>
            <td>—</td>
            <td class="tot">{수(data.men)}</td>
            <td class="tot">{수(data.women)}</td>
            <td>{수(data.sexNotRecorded)}</td>
            <td class="tot">{수(data.distinctPeopleWithBirthYear)}</td>
          </tr>
          {있는해.map((y) => (
            <tr class={y.해나이 >= 24 && y.해나이 <= 30 ? 'edge' : ''}>
              <td class="nm">{y.생년}</td>
              <td>{y.해나이}</td>
              <td class="tot">{수(y.남성)}</td>
              <td>{수(y.여성)}</td>
              <td class="fine">{수(y.성별미확인)}</td>
              <td>{수(y.전체)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The single largest cohort of men in the roster was born in <b>{가장많은해.생년}</b> —
      {수(가장많은해.남성)} of them, turning {가장많은해.해나이} during {해}. Across the birth years that
      turn 24 to 30 this year there are <b>{수(남성합)}</b> men, which is
      {' '}{Math.round(남성합 / Math.max(1, data.men) * 100)}% of all {수(data.men)} men we could count.
      That is a statement about who was recorded, not about who is due for anything.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sex is recorded for {성별율}% of them — the rest stay blank</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Of {수(data.distinctPeopleWithBirthYear)} members, {수(data.men + data.women)} have a sex or gender
      recorded and <b>{수(data.sexNotRecorded)} do not</b>. We leave that column blank rather than
      guessing from a name or a group, because a guess would be our judgement wearing the source's
      clothes. Any share you compute from the men and women columns is a share of the recorded part,
      not of the roster.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where we refuse to give a number</h2>
    <p class="note">
      <b>We do not publish a list of the men on their own.</b> The counts are here by birth year, and
      names appear on our birth-year pages alongside everyone born that year. A men-only list ordered
      by age would read as a conscription schedule, which is not what this data is and not something
      we are in a position to publish about named people.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>Place of birth is not citizenship.</b> Some members of Korean groups were born outside Korea,
      and some born in Korea hold another passport. Wikidata records a birthplace for only part of
      the roster and never records citizenship for this purpose, so no nationality split appears above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/service-years" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from, and what they cannot answer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Wikidata (CC0)</b> — {data.source}</li>
      <li>
        <b>Members are people who were in the group.</b> Wikidata's member property does not separate
        current members from former ones, so someone who left years ago is still counted here.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>A bigger year means more people were recorded.</b> It does not mean more people debuted.
        Recent years are written up more thoroughly than old ones.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>We do not hold:</b> {data.weDoNotHave.join(' · ')}.
      </li>
      <li><b>Built {data.builtOn}, as of {해}.</b> Rebuild moves every age, never a birth year.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/born-year">Korean entertainers by birth year</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/group">Korean groups we track</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
